cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the released model outputs, please cite the paper."
title: "Resolution Without Relations: Quantifying the Perception-Reasoning Trade-off of Tile Selection in Ultra-High-Resolution Remote Sensing"
abstract: >-
  Code, per-item model outputs and analysis for a controlled study of question-relevant tile
  selection in ultra-high-resolution remote sensing visual question answering. Selection improves
  perception accuracy and degrades spatial relational accuracy; supplying the discarded layout as
  an explicit relation graph, under matched VLM calls and encoded pixels, does not recover it.
